=== W1 Item 6: text_width Underflow Verification Log ===
Date: 2026-11-03
Agent: antigravity (Chat A2)

1. Description of Defect & Resolution:
Defect (W1 #6, defect #10):
`framebuffer.rs::text_width()` computed `chars * 9 - 1`. On an empty string `""`, `chars` is 0. With `overflow-checks = true` in release profile (`kernel/Cargo.toml`), computing `0u64 * 9 - 1` triggers an arithmetic underflow panic.

Resolution:
- Confirmed `kernel/src/framebuffer.rs` computes width using saturating arithmetic:
  `chars.saturating_mul(9).saturating_sub(1)`
  An empty string returns width 0 without panic.
- Added committed selftest function `test_text_width_underflow()` in `framebuffer.rs` wired into `memselftest::phase4()`:
  * Asserts `dummy.text_width("") == 0`
  * Asserts `dummy.text_width("A") == 8`
  * Asserts `dummy.text_width("AB") == 17`
- Updated `kernel/src/panic.rs` to invoke `qemu_exit::failure()` under `cfg(feature = "qemu-exit")` before halting, ensuring any panic in selftest cleanly triggers QEMU debug exit code 35 (`NOVA_SELFTEST_FAILED`).
- Verified failure on plant:
  * In a scratch clone outside the repo, reverted `text_width` to `chars * 9 - 1`.
  * `dummy.text_width("")` panicked on underflow (`attempt to subtract with overflow`).
  * Panic handler caught the defect and QEMU exited with code 35 (`NOVA_SELFTEST_FAILED`).

